; MX2 the transfers (README "MX2"). Each routine is the data book's formula as its first draft
; (the book check: the routine's clocks to the FLUSH, the refill's first fetch at W = 0, the E
; word and its post-E word); where silicon's events (the frozen model, exact on the run named)
; place the FLUSH later, the extra words are OPEN and declared "silicon longer than the book".
;
; The acts (one a word unless merged):
;   the target's add      SIGMA <- PC + the displacement (SR_PC: the instruction pointer, the
;                         byte after the routine's last pop; IMM: the displacement, a byte
;                         sign-extended (the short forms' format) or a word)
;   the decide            a jump on the format's condition (CD_XC: the PSW's sixteen for 70-7F,
;                         the counter tests of the loop forms on SIGMA) or on SIGMA (CD_SNZ)
;   fw                    the not-taken decide's wait: while a fetch cycle runs or delivers its
;                         word (the frozen model's untaken=wait, nfgap 1)
;   SUSP                  prefetching suspended from the word to the FLUSH; the word waits while
;                         a fetch cycle runs (the V20 ROM's SUSP; the model's flush_held and the
;                         flush's gap after the last fetch)
;   FLUSH                 the queue and the staging register emptied, the stream from SIGMA in PS
;                         (the queue's flush; the refill's first fetch issues on its clock)
;   E                     after a FLUSH it pops the target's opcode once the refill's fetch run
;                         has ended (the sequencer's refill gate: no fetch in flight, the line
;                         down at the last clock's end)
; A short transfer's displacement is popped by the E word with its opcode (the decode's e2: the
; model's take on the start clock) and arms the take sync: the routine's first word waits for
; the word the pop's room asked for (the model's exec clocks start on its delivery).

; ---- BR short (EB): V20 JMP short 0158-015B (Q -> tmpbL, SUSP, PC -> tmpa, SIGMA -> PC FLUSH)
routine br_short op=EB book="BR short-label" diff=-1 why="OPEN: book error of one in the book check's machine (nine words, the E word waiting for the refill's first fetch issued on the flush's clock: 11; on silicon the target's fetch starts five clocks after the flush and the dispatch waits for four bytes, the qprobe j0 / j1 runs); (qprobe rule 6) BR short is `. . . P . . F N .`: the displacement released on the fourth word, F (the flush, the seventh) waits while a fetch cycle runs (rule 5: nothing is fetched after it and the target's fetch starts five clocks later, the queue's flush wait), N the eighth (waits for the target's byte), E the ninth (waits for four bytes of the new stream: the sequencer's rule 4c): 9 (the qprobe j0 / j1 runs, all exact; F23-push-br-n0-pE-w0's flush six after the last fetch's end is rule 5's wait and latency); the book's 12 places the flush later; the target's add, two words with no act, the release, two more, FLUSH, E"
    alu=ADD ax=PC ay=IMM                    ; the target: the instruction pointer + the displacement
    open call=w1                            ; OPEN: a book clock with no act (BR short 12) (2 clocks: the call and the shared delay's 1)
    rl=1                                    ; (qprobe rule 3) P: the displacement (popped by the E word with the opcode) released
    open call=w1                            ; OPEN: a book clock with no act (BR short 12) (2 clocks: the call and the shared delay's 1)
    flush bi                                ; FLUSH: the stream from the target; (qprobe rule 5) waits while a fetch cycle runs
    e ro                                    ; E: the target's opcode, once delivered; (qprobe) ro: released

; ---- Bcond (70-7F): V20 JCC 0034-0039 (Q -> tmpbL ALU ADD, JMP OPC, E; taken SUSP, FLUSH E)
routine bcond op=70-7F book="BC/BZ/BNZ/BNC short-label (Bcond)" diff=nt:+0,t:+0 why="OPEN: (qprobe round 10, Q27) not taken `. . . BP . . BN .`, taken `. . . BP . . . B . . F N .` (the qprobe jz / jnz and ic-* / id-* runs): the fourth word (the decide, the displacement released) is bus-idle: behind a short predecessor at an even address it waits for the fetch its own opcode's pop started; taken, a second bus-idle word four words after the displacement; the target's add, two words with no act, the decide (BP); not taken two words with no act, E (BN); taken three words with no act, B, two words with no act, FLUSH (F), E; the book's 8 and 15"
    alu=ADD ax=PC ay=IMM call=w2            ; the target: the instruction pointer + the displacement; OPEN words: (qprobe round 10) the second and third words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 2)
    jc=XC:bc_t rl=1 bi                      ; the decide: the condition on the PSW (the encoding's); (qprobe round 10, Q27) B P: bus-idle (waits while a pin cycle started earlier runs), the displacement released
    open call=w1                            ; OPEN: (qprobe round 10) not taken: two words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 1)
    e bi ro                                 ; not taken: E; (qprobe) bi: bus-idle; ro: the next opcode released (B N)
bc_t: open call=w2                          ; OPEN: (qprobe round 10) taken: three words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 2)
    bi                                      ; (qprobe round 10, Q27) taken: B, four words after the displacement
    open call=w1                            ; OPEN: (qprobe round 10) taken: two words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 1)
    flush bi                                ; FLUSH: the stream from the target; (qprobe rule 5) waits while a pin cycle runs
    e ro                                    ; E: the target's opcode, once delivered; (qprobe) ro: released

; ---- BR near (E9): V20 JMP near 0154-0157 (Q -> tmpbL, Q -> tmpbH, PC -> tmpa SUSP, FLUSH E)
routine br_near op=E9 book="BR near-label" why="OPEN: (qprobe round 8, Q21) BR near is `. . . . PP . . F N .` (the qprobe fl-jn / fl-jn1 / jn runs): the displacement popped on the fourth and fifth words and released on the fifth, the target's add, two words with no act, F (the flush, bus-idle: waits while a fetch's pin cycle runs) three clocks after the last input, N, the dispatch; the target's fetch five clocks after the flush word (the queue's flush wait): one tail for every transfer; the book's 12 in the book check's machine; before round 8: the immediate's latency, the pops, the add, SUSP, FLUSH, E (F23-push-brnear-n0-pE-w0)"
    open call=w2                            ; OPEN: (qprobe round 8) a word with no act (3 clocks: the call and the shared delay's 2)
    pop=il                                  ; pop the displacement's low byte (its release is the next word's)
    pop=ih rl=2                             ; pop its high byte; (qprobe round 8) PP: both displacement bytes released
    alu=ADD ax=PC ay=IMM                    ; the target: the instruction pointer + the displacement
    open                                    ; OPEN: (qprobe round 8) a word with no act
    flush bi                                ; FLUSH: the stream from the target; (qprobe rule 5) waits while a fetch's pin cycle runs
    e ro                                    ; E: the target's opcode, once delivered; (qprobe) ro: released

; ---- DBNZ (E2): V20 LOOP 013C-013F, 0138-013B (CX - 1, JMP NZ; PC + disp, FLUSH E)
routine dbnz op=E2 book="DBNZ" lead=2 diff=t:+0,nt:+2 why="OPEN: silicon longer than the book (measured, the extra words OPEN): (qprobe round 10, Q27 / Q28) DBNZ is taken `. . . B . . P . . B . . F N .`, not taken `. . . B . . P . BN .`, with lead 2 (its boundary no sooner than two clocks after its opcode's release: the decode's lead, MOV sreg,r's; the qprobe id-* / ie-* runs): CW - 1, CW written, a word with no act, B (the bus-idle fourth word), two words with no act, the displacement released (P) and the count test; not taken a word with no act, E bus-idle (BN); taken a word with no act, the target's add, B (three words after the displacement), two words with no act, FLUSH (F), E"
    rb=CW wid=WORD alu=DEC ax=RB            ; CW - 1 (no flags)
    wr=CW wid=WORD ws=SIG call=w1           ; CW <- CW - 1; OPEN: (qprobe round 10) the third word with no act (the call and the shared delay's 1)
dbnz_b: bi call=w2                          ; (qprobe round 10, Q27) B: the bus-idle fourth word; OPEN: two words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 2)
    jc=SNZ:dbnz_t rl=1                      ; the count test (taken while CW - 1, in SIGMA since the first word, is not zero; DBNZE / DBNZNE's too); P: the displacement (popped by the E word with the opcode) released
dbnz_n: open                                ; OPEN: (qprobe round 10) not taken: a word with no act
    e bi ro                                 ; E (not taken); bi: bus-idle; ro: the next opcode released (B N)
dbnz_t: alu=ADD ax=PC ay=IMM                ; taken: the target: the instruction pointer + the displacement
    open                                    ; OPEN: (qprobe round 10) taken: a word with no act
    bi call=w2                              ; (qprobe round 10, Q24) taken: B, three words after the displacement; OPEN: two words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 2)
    flush bi                                ; FLUSH: the stream from the target (bus-idle)
    e ro                                    ; E: the target's opcode, once delivered; ro: released

; ---- DBNZNE / DBNZE (E0 / E1): V20 LOOPNZ / LOOPZ 0134-013B (JMP REP: the count and Z)
routine dbnz_z op=E0,E1 book="DBNZE" diff=t:1,nt:0 why="OPEN: silicon longer than the book (measured, the extra words OPEN): (qprobe round 13, Q43) DBNZE / DBNZNE (E1 / E0) are not DBNZ's routine and have no lead (the qprobe dbnze runs, 60 / 60): taken `. . . B . . . P . . B . . F N .`; not taken with the flag false and CW not 0 `. . . B . . PN .` (BCWZ's not-taken routine); CW 0 with the flag true `. . . B . . . P . BN .`; CW 0 with the flag false `. . . B P . BN .`"
    rb=CW wid=WORD alu=DEC ax=RB            ; CW - 1 (no flags)
    wr=CW wid=WORD ws=SIG                   ; CW <- CW - 1
    jnc=SNZ:dz_z0                           ; the count test (CW - 1 zero: the count's exits)
    bi jnc=XC:dz_b                          ; (qprobe round 13, Q43) B: the bus-idle fourth word; the flag test (DBNZNE continues on NZ, DBNZE on Z): false, the flag's exit
    alu=ADD ax=PC ay=IMM                    ; taken: the target: the instruction pointer + the displacement
    open call=w1                            ; OPEN: (qprobe round 13, Q43) taken: two words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 1)
    rl=1                                    ; (qprobe round 13, Q43) P: the displacement released (the eighth word)
    open call=w1                            ; OPEN: (qprobe round 13, Q43) two words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 1)
    bi                                      ; (qprobe round 13, Q43) B: three words after the displacement
    open call=w1                            ; OPEN: (qprobe round 13, Q43) two words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 1)
    flush bi                                ; FLUSH: the stream from the target (bus-idle)
    e ro                                    ; E: the target's opcode, once delivered; ro: released
dz_b: open call=w1                          ; OPEN: (qprobe round 13, Q43) not taken, the flag false: two words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 1)
    e ro rl=1                               ; E: P N: the displacement and the next opcode released
dz_z0: bi jnc=XC:dz_d                       ; (qprobe round 13, Q43) B: the bus-idle fourth word (CW 0); the flag test
    open call=w2                            ; OPEN: (qprobe round 13, Q43) CW 0, the flag true: three words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 2)
    rl=1                                    ; (qprobe round 13, Q43) P: the displacement released
    open                                    ; OPEN: (qprobe round 13, Q43) a word with no act
    e ro bi                                 ; E: B N
dz_d: rl=1                                  ; (qprobe round 13, Q43) CW 0, the flag false: P (the fifth word)
    open                                    ; OPEN: (qprobe round 13, Q43) a word with no act
    e ro bi                                 ; E: B N

