; ---- BRK 3 (CC) / BRK imm8 (CD) / BRKV (CE): V20 INT3 0104, INT_N 0108, INTO 010C + INT 01EC-01FC
; (the vector's two reads from segment 0, PSW pushed with IE and BRK cleared (CITF), PS and PC
; pushed, PS and PC loaded, FLUSH E). The type byte popped as a port number (no take sync: the
; frozen model's chained take); BRKV's V test (the format's condition, 70's)
routine brk_imm op=CD book="BRK imm8" diff=1 why="OPEN: silicon longer than the book (measured, the extra words OPEN): (qprobe round 13, Q44) BRK imm8 is `. . . BP . B . . Y` then INT 3's sequence from its first request (the qprobe tr-brk runs): the type byte taken on the fourth word (bus idle), a second bus-idle word two later"
